## Overview

This PR addresses code duplication in the veto competition flow by extracting repeated Final 4 detection logic into a reusable helper function.

## Problem

The Final 4 detection logic was duplicated in both the success and error branches of the `showVetoRevealSequence` promise handler in `js/veto.js`. This violated the DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) principle and made the code harder to maintain.

**Before:**
```javascript
showVetoRevealSequence(top3).then(function(){
  var aliveCount = alivePlayers().length;
  if(aliveCount === 4){
    setTimeout(function(){ startFinal4Eviction(); }, 500);
  } else {
    setTimeout(function(){ startVetoCeremony(); }, 500);
  }
}).catch(function(e){
  console.warn('[veto] reveal error, proceeding', e);
  var aliveCount = alivePlayers().length;
  if(aliveCount === 4){
    setTimeout(function(){ startFinal4Eviction(); }, 500);
  } else {
    setTimeout(function(){ startVetoCeremony(); }, 500);
  }
});
```

## Solution

Extracted the duplicated logic into a new `handlePostVetoReveal()` helper function that is called from both branches:

**After:**
```javascript
function handlePostVetoReveal(){
  var aliveCount = alivePlayers().length;
  if(aliveCount === 4){
    setTimeout(function(){ startFinal4Eviction(); }, 500);
  } else {
    setTimeout(function(){ startVetoCeremony(); }, 500);
  }
}

showVetoRevealSequence(top3).then(function(){
  handlePostVetoReveal();
}).catch(function(e){
  console.warn('[veto] reveal error, proceeding', e);
  handlePostVetoReveal();
});
```

## Benefits

- ✅ **Eliminates code duplication** - Single source of truth for Final 4 detection logic
- ✅ **Improves maintainability** - Future changes only need to be made in one place
- ✅ **Reduces code size** - Net reduction of 1 line (11 insertions, 12 deletions)
- ✅ **Better readability** - Clear function name documents intent
- ✅ **Consistent behavior** - Ensures both branches execute identical logic

## Testing

All existing tests pass:
- ✅ Minigame key validation
- ✅ Legacy map validation
- ✅ Runtime validation
- ✅ E2E validation

## Code Quality

The implementation follows existing code conventions:
- Uses `var` declarations consistent with the rest of the file
- Maintains function hoisting patterns
- Preserves exact behavior including 500ms timeout
- No functional changes, only structural refactoring

Closes issue requesting extraction of duplicated Final 4 detection logic.

